- How would you extend to non-uniform block counts or dynamic block that isn't divisor of 128?
- How to optimize for block=16 across many values in tight loops?

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes fluency with SWAR bit-twiddling and 128-bit composition, ensuring branchless correctness.

## Key Concepts
- 64-bit SWAR reversal
- 128-bit result from {hi: rev64(lo), lo: rev64(hi)}
- Mask/shift sequences to flip bit blocks without branches

## Code Example
```c
static inline uint64_t rev64(uint64_t x){
  x = (x >> 1) & 0x5555555555555555ULL | (x & 0x5555555555555555ULL) << 1;
  x = (x >> 2) & 0x3333333333333333ULL | (x & 0x3333333333333333ULL) << 2;
  x = (x >> 4) & 0x0F0F0F0F0F0F0F0FULL | (x & 0x0F0F0F0F0F0F0F0FULL) << 4;
  x = (x >> 8) & 0x00FF00FF00FF00FFULL | (x & 0x00FF00FF00FF00FFULL) << 8;
  x = (x >> 16) & 0x0000FFFF0000FFFFULL | (x & 0x0000FFFF0000FFFFULL) << 16;
  x = (x >> 32) | (x << 32);
  return x;
}

uint128 reverseBits128(uint128 x){
  uint128 r;
  r.hi = rev64(x.lo);
  r.lo = rev64(x.hi);
  return r;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test edge alignment and performance implications?
- Could this approach be generalized to arbitrary widths with minimal changes?

## Why This Question Is Asked
This question tests advanced bit manipulation skills. A palindrome check requires full 128-bit reversal and a single branchless comparison. It assesses understanding of endianness, cross-lane bit operations, and how to compose a complex operation from a reusable primitive.

## Key Concepts
- 128-bit bit reversal (SWAR-style steps)
- Branchless comparison via bitwise XOR
- Endian-agnostic bit ordering across two 64-bit lanes

## Code Example
```c
int isBitPalindrome128(uint128 x) {
    uint128 r = reverseBits128(x);
    uint128 d = x ^ r;
    return (d == 0) ? 1 : 0;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of compact bit-twiddling techniques to count bits without loops, a common interview staple for performance-critical code.

## Key Concepts

- Parallel bit counting (SIMD-style within a register)
- Bit masks and shifts for aggregation
- Portability across unsigned integers and compilers

## Code Example

```c
uint32_t popcount32(uint32_t n) {
  n = n - ((n >> 1) & 0x55555555);
  n = (n & 0x33333333) + ((n >> 2) & 0x33333333);
  n = (n + (n >> 4)) & 0x0F0F0F0F;
  return (n * 0x01010101) >> 24;
}
```

