## Why This Is Asked
Tests crossing-boundary bit extraction on a 128-bit value with no branching, mirroring real-world crypto/low-level data parsing tasks.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-boundary bit manipulation.
- Mask generation for widths up to 64 without 64-bit overflow.
- Handling 128-bit values via hi/lo halves (no loops).

## Code Example
```javascript
function extractBits128(hi, lo, pos, width) {
  const V = (BigInt(hi) << 64n) | BigInt(lo);
  const mask = width === 64 ? (1n << 64n) - 1n : (1n << BigInt(width)) - 1n;
  return (V >> BigInt(pos)) & mask;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests extending known 64-bit tricks to 128-bit values with branchless code.

## Key Concepts
- Branchless bit counting
- 64-bit popcount kernel
- Combining results across two words

## Code Example
```c
static inline uint64_t popcount64(uint64_t x){
  x -= (x >> 1) & 0x5555555555555555ULL;
  x = (x & 0x3333333333333333ULL) + ((x >> 2) & 0x3333333333333333ULL);
  x = (x + (x >> 4)) & 0x0F0F0F0F0F0F0F0FULL;
  return (x * 0x0101010101010101ULL) >> 56;
}

uint8_t popcount128(uint64_t hi, uint64_t lo){
  return (uint8_t)(popcount64(hi) + popcount64(lo));
}
```

